Go IDE boundary stays upstream GOPACKAGESDRIVER on rules_go 0.63.0:
pure-Go packages including declared build constraints and platform source selection
through the pinned driver rather than creating a static package snapshot or
replacement package graph; Use a separate IDE output base with do not mutate the
selected environment; propagate failures rather than reporting a successful
incomplete package graph.
cgo completion is out of scope and this exception does not admit the complete Go
foundation: upstream does not guarantee cgo completion, so record cgo and platform
gaps rather than claiming generic IDE parity.

Rejected: third-party plugin claim plus private first-party contribution path plus
